1
00:00:00,174 --> 00:00:04,294
India and China trade about
118 billion dollars a year.

2
00:00:04,294 --> 00:00:05,464
What if it all stopped?

3
00:00:05,655 --> 00:00:07,425
India buys far more than it sells.

4
00:00:07,555 --> 00:00:10,505
The gap is roughly 85
billion dollars a year.

5
00:00:10,521 --> 00:00:14,471
Phone parts, solar panels,
machines and chemicals come in from China.

6
00:00:14,626 --> 00:00:18,686
Even India's medicine makers depend on
China for a large share of their raw

7
00:00:18,686 --> 00:00:22,136
ingredients,
often cited at around 70 percent.

8
00:00:22,562 --> 00:00:25,432
A sudden stop would hit factories first,
then prices.

9
00:00:25,707 --> 00:00:30,177
China would lose a big market too,
but India is a small share of its exports.

10
00:00:30,377 --> 00:00:34,507
Over time India could shift to Vietnam,
Taiwan, Korea and its own plants,

11
00:00:34,857 --> 00:00:35,987
but that takes years.

12
00:00:36,143 --> 00:00:38,673
Should India cut its
dependence on Chinese goods?

13
00:00:38,838 --> 00:00:39,468
Comment.

